The package kurlyk provides the CMake target:

    find_package(kurlyk CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE kurlyk::kurlyk)

The package requires C++11 or later. Its HTTP and WebSocket transports use the
vcpkg-provided curl, OpenSSL, Asio, and Simple-WebSocket-Server dependencies.

The default port is built with standalone Asio. Selecting Boost.Asio for the
exported `kurlyk::kurlyk` target requires building Kurlyk from source with
`KURLYK_USE_STANDALONE_ASIO=OFF`; the installed vcpkg package does not switch
backend after configuration. The standalone `simple-websocket-server` port
provides an additive `boost-asio` feature for consumers using SWS directly.
